  "chapter": 651,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 33 Chapter 651\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 4727, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  workers'  compensation law, in relation to\n        extending paid family leave benefits\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would create a new  eligibility  standard  for  paid  family\nleave  benefits for construction employees who work for multiple employ-\ners pursuant to a collective bargaining agreement. Such employees  would\nbecome  eligible  for paid family leave benefits after employment for at\nleast twenty-six of the last thirty-nine weeks with any employer who  is\na  signatory to a collective bargaining agreement, including upon return\nto work if such employees were laid off and received unemployment  bene-\nfits, but otherwise were in employment at least 26 of the last 39 weeks.\n \n  I  support  extending  access  to  paid family leave benefits to these\nconstruction employees who may have difficulty gaining eligibility  with\na  single  employer.  However,  changes  were necessary to clarify which\nemployer is responsible when a paid family leave claim is  made  and  to\naddress  the  availability  of health insurance benefits while on family\nleave. Additionally, the bill's immediate effective date did not provide\ntime for the Workers' Compensation Board to make  necessary  administra-\ntive and regulatory changes.\n \n  I  have  secured an agreement with the Legislature to enact changes to\naddress these issues in  the  upcoming  legislative  session,  including\nextending  the  effective  date to January 1, 2027. On the basis of this\nagreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2025
 },
